1
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:10,760
<i>Round 21 will now begin.</i>

2
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:14,014
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

3
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:15,098
MYSTERY STOCK MARKET

4
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:16,474
What happened to Shindong?

5
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:18,143
11TH PLACE: JUNG WON-YOUNG
12TH PLACE: SHINDONG

6
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,937
What happened to Shindong?
What's going on?

7
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:22,188
What happened?

8
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:23,898
What happened to Shindong?

9
00:00:24,941 --> 00:00:26,192
How does that make sense?

10
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:31,906
What the?

11
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:33,700
What happened?

12
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,746
What did you do?

13
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:46,254
Damn it. Why'd you do that?

14
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:49,382
I'm sorry.

15
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:59,517
15 HOURS AGO

16
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:06,399
<i>Jung Won-young,</i>

17
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:11,071
<i>you have been cursed by the barrier</i>

18
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:14,282
<i>that was guarding the prize token.</i>

19
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:17,243
<i>Those who have been cursed</i>

20
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:20,538
<i>lose every Piece they hold</i>

21
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:23,875
<i>and will not be able to</i>

22
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:29,380
<i>acquire or use any Pieces</i>
<i>in </i>The Devil's Plan.

23
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,927
<i>To break the curse,</i>

24
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:37,889
<i>the one person you choose</i>

25
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:43,103
<i>must be eliminated</i>
<i>in tomorrow's main match.</i>

26
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:52,654
<i>Please choose one person</i>

27
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:57,992
<i>to eliminate in tomorrow's main match.</i>

28
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:00,703
<i>You cannot choose yourself,</i>

29
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:03,748
<i>and the player you choose</i>
<i>must be a player of the living area.</i>

30
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:23,393
<i>Who do you choose</i>
<i>as the player to be eliminated tomorrow?</i>

31
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:29,816
Kyung-lyul has two Pieces,

32
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:32,277
Hyun-min has two,
and Dong-min has four… No, five.

33
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,320
I had no idea
what the next main match would be,

34
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,488
but Pieces could be involved,

35
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:38,533
so I thought I should choose someone
with only one Piece.

36
00:02:39,325 --> 00:02:41,161
Jang Dong-min and Oh Hyun-min.

37
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,956
Hyun-min isn't an option since he has two.

38
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,082
Dong-jae?

39
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,252
Dong-jae…

40
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:54,674
<i>Second, I thought</i>
<i>that it'd be too hard for me</i>

41
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:55,842
<i>to control Dong-min's inner circle.</i>

42
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:59,137
<i>So I ruled out Dong-jae and Hyun-min,</i>
<i>who are the closest to him.</i>

43
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:02,849
<i>I also excluded Kyung-lyul</i>
<i>because he has two Pieces.</i>

44
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:04,934
Yurisa…

45
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:10,315
<i>That left me with Yurisa and Shindong.</i>

46
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:11,983
Shindong…

47
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:16,237
I want you to stay.

48
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:17,447
Up.

49
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,907
Light up my back.

50
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:21,242
I want Won-young to go.

51
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:22,368
Me too.

52
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:34,172
I choose Shindong.

53
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:38,009
I believed my bond with Shindong
was strong enough

54
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:41,054
<i>that he'd trust me more than the others.</i>

55
00:03:41,554 --> 00:03:46,226
<i>If Shindong is eliminated</i>
<i>in the main match,</i>

56
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:50,605
<i>you will be freed from the curse</i>

57
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:55,109
<i>and receive a salvation token.</i>

58
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:57,445
<i>The salvation token</i>

59
00:03:57,528 --> 00:04:01,282
<i>is an item that saves you</i>
<i>when you are eliminated,</i>

60
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:05,286
<i>allowing you to continue</i>
<i>as a player in prison.</i>

61
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:08,831
<i>And if you become a player in prison,</i>

62
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:14,128
<i>it will allow you</i>
<i>to move up to the living area.</i>

63
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:16,547
<i>The salvation token</i>

64
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:22,095
<i>is usable through the end</i>
<i>of the fifth main match</i>

65
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:27,809
<i>and can be transferred to another player.</i>

66
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:34,065
<i>However, it cannot be transferred</i>
<i>to Shindong.</i>

67
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:38,152
If two players aren't eliminated tomorrow,
I end up cursed.

68
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:39,737
Won-young.

69
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:41,322
Yes?

70
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:43,825
You can't trick me.

71
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:50,206
<i>Yesterday, the players in the living area</i>
<i>decided to prioritize our group's survival</i>

72
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:52,792
and eliminate two other players
from prison.

73
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:54,961
I had a feeling
things might not go my way,

74
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:56,879
so I needed an ally.

75
00:04:56,963 --> 00:05:00,425
If you won't tell even me the truth,

76
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:02,176
no one can help you.

77
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,513
Before it gets any more dangerous for you,

78
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,224
you should at least be honest with me.

79
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,851
When it comes to the curse,

80
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:13,688
- you're the only person I can trust.
- Right.

81
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:16,441
- Are you gonna tell me the truth now?
- Yes.

82
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:20,403
I had to choose someone
from the living area to be eliminated

83
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:21,863
in today's main match.

84
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:22,947
Okay.

85
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:23,990
So,

86
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:26,367
I chose Shindong.

87
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:34,751
I never imagined he had to pick someone
from the living area.

88
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:39,672
It hit me that anyone there
could end up in this situation.

89
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,216
So I felt for him,

90
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,845
and I somewhat came to understand
why he lied yesterday.

91
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:47,722
If it hadn't been Shindong,

92
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:50,266
I would've helped without hesitation.

93
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:51,684
If you had

94
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,354
chosen anyone else,

95
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,314
I would've totally helped you.

96
00:05:57,148 --> 00:06:01,986
But I told Shindong last night
that we'd do this together.

97
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,781
You trusted me enough to tell me,

98
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:07,200
so I won't tell anyone about this.

99
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:09,702
I won't say anything to Shindong either.

100
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:12,330
And if people start suspecting you,

101
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:14,415
I'll smooth that over for you.

102
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:19,629
I know what you need most is my help,

103
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,422
but the extent to which I can help

104
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:24,342
is taking the heat off you,
getting the others to trust you,

105
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:27,387
and getting Shindong
to play alongside you.

106
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:29,013
But the rest is up to you.

107
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:34,560
1 HOUR AGO

108
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:37,563
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

109
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,065
John.

110
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:43,486
We need some safe gains.
Should we wash trade Analog Electronics?

111
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:46,155
When you're low on cash,
go to Analog Electronics.

112
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:47,740
Electronics offers
an extra 1,500 won per trade,

113
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:51,035
but Open Security
gives you a 13% gain on its price.

114
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,954
You can increase your assets more quickly
with Analog Electronics.

115
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,665
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

116
00:06:56,707 --> 00:07:00,336
I have to take Shindong down,
push the others up from last place,

117
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,879
and I have to stay alive too.

118
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:04,048
I don't know how many plays
I'm running right now.

119
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:06,801
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

120
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:09,637
- We'll buy NotSoGood Capital--
- Do I sell everything and buy it?

121
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,847
Yeah. Sell Banger Steel.

122
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:13,224
Sorry, but can I buy CoyoTech?

123
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:14,767
- Be our guest.
- Go ahead.

124
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:15,685
It's because I'm last.

125
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:17,687
BANGER STEEL: 7 SHARES
OPEN SECURITY: 1 SHARE

126
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,397
BOUGHT

127
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,232
ANALOG ELECTRONICS
SECRET

128
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:23,025
<i>That concludes Round 14.</i>

129
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,987
- Let's see now.
<i>- Round 15 will now begin.</i>

130
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:28,573
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

131
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:29,699
It went down.

132
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:32,618
If Mucho Construction dropped,
we failed, right?

133
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:33,703
- Yeah, we did.
- Yeah.

134
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:36,205
Did they sell? Or did they buy too?

135
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:39,083
I bought Banger Steel
and blocked it in the last round.

136
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,502
They were going all in
on NotSoGood Capital to get a 20% gain,

137
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:42,753
so I had to block it.

138
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,881
Who put the secret
on Analog Electronics this round?

139
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,799
Who put the secret on Analog Electronics?

140
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:48,217
It wasn't us.

141
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:49,135
I thought it was you guys.

142
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:51,429
<i>Round 16 will now begin.</i>

143
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:54,348
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

144
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:56,309
8TH: SHINDONG,
10TH: JUNG WON-YOUNG, 12TH: YURISA

145
00:07:56,392 --> 00:08:00,563
I think my brain just hit its limit.
I couldn't do anything right.

146
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:04,275
<i>I started thinking,</i>
<i>"Am I really just gonna get eliminated?"</i>

147
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:05,193
Shindong.

148
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:08,029
- I have to come in last
- Yeah?

149
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:09,489
in the main match this time.

150
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:12,200
Last place gets an advantage.

151
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:15,620
You have to get eliminated?

152
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:16,537
I have to place last.

153
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:18,748
You should've told me that sooner.

154
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:21,042
That's why I stayed at the bottom.
Bet you never guessed.

155
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:23,961
I was wondering
why that was happening.

156
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:27,924
The sacrifice token activates
when you're in the bottom two.

157
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:31,677
The optimal setup for this token
is one in prison and one in last place.

158
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:34,305
For this token, the prison token.

159
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:36,474
- So we need to finish 11th and 12th, then.
- Yeah.

160
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:39,101
But Yurisa keeps ending up in last place.

161
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,978
Then you should tell her too.

162
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,730
- You can share this with her too, right?
- No.

163
00:08:42,813 --> 00:08:44,941
- No?
- Only two players can use it.

164
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:47,693
- So did you choose me or--
- I did.

165
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,070
When you were in there?

166
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:52,782
Why didn't you tell me this sooner?

167
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:58,079
<i>Because Shindong has trusted me</i>
<i>since the very first day of this game,</i>

168
00:08:58,162 --> 00:09:00,456
the strategy I came up with on the spot

169
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,418
was to lie about the token's effect
and push him into last place.

170
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:07,338
Then we both go to the living area
and get a token.

171
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:08,881
<i>Turns out there's a new rule.</i>

172
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,925
<i>But honestly, I've got nothing to lose.</i>

173
00:09:11,008 --> 00:09:12,468
<i>I was headed to prison either way.</i>

174
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:16,180
I only need to avoid finishing last,
so I'm gonna trust him and go for it.

175
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:19,058
I don't know why my heart
is pounding right now.

176
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:23,688
It's a bit late, but should we try
working on Banger Steel?

177
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:25,565
The last gamble.

178
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,942
You should buy Security, Yurisa.

179
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:29,318
- Security?
- Yes, for 13%.

180
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,653
Open Security.

181
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:31,779
- Buy it?
- Yes.

182
00:09:31,862 --> 00:09:32,863
- It's going up.
- Move up the rankings.

183
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:35,616
<i>Round 17 will now begin.</i>

184
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:38,661
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

185
00:09:38,744 --> 00:09:41,205
My going down is fine,
but you're sitting way too high right now.

186
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,290
Okay.

187
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:43,416
What do you suggest we do?

188
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:45,543
We need to go for what's dropping.

189
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:49,380
Can't we just go with the strategy
of building up Banger Steel?

190
00:09:49,463 --> 00:09:51,841
I just bought ten shares of Banger Steel.

191
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:55,761
You need to load up on Construction
and sell Open Security.

192
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:58,014
<i>Round 18 will now begin.</i>

193
00:09:58,097 --> 00:10:00,891
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

194
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,269
Good. We need to maintain this.

195
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:06,480
<i>Round 19 will now begin.</i>

196
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:09,191
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

197
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:12,528
- How did you jump in the rankings?
- Both stocks went up.

198
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:15,781
Mucho Construction and Banger Steel
suddenly went up.

199
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:17,867
- Damn it.
- Banger Steel…

200
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:20,870
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

201
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:22,622
Wait, why did Shindong go down?

202
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,415
Alt Ent would've doubled if you invested.

203
00:10:24,498 --> 00:10:26,125
Yeah, why didn't you?

204
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:27,460
I told you to buy it.

205
00:10:27,543 --> 00:10:29,253
It's too obvious.

206
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:31,922
Everyone is asking
why I didn't buy Alt Ent.

207
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:36,594
Let's put everything we've got
into Analog Electronics this round.

208
00:10:37,219 --> 00:10:38,596
Then we can tank it.

209
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:41,849
<i>Analog Electronics has a rule</i>
<i>that drops its value by 1,000 won,</i>

210
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:44,644
and its current price
is sitting in the 1,000 won range.

211
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:48,856
<i>If it hits the floor at 100 won,</i>
<i>that's a -90%.</i>

212
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:52,193
It seemed like my last chance
to get a cut that steep,

213
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:53,569
so I pushed hard for it.

214
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:56,864
This is the -90% moment
where 1,000 drops to 100.

215
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:58,366
This is the golden opportunity.

216
00:10:58,449 --> 00:11:02,787
Outside of this, it'll just stay at 100
because the floor price is set.

217
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:05,247
This is our one chance
to make it crash hard in one shot.

218
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,500
Let's do it.

219
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,127
First, sell everything.
Then only buy Electronics.

220
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,505
Okay, I did it.

221
00:11:12,588 --> 00:11:15,341
I'll buy 16 more.

222
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:18,260
Then you'll be sitting
at around 40,000 won,

223
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:20,137
and I'll be at around 30,000 won.

224
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,139
- Let's go.
- Let's.

225
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:24,308
Should we sit there?

226
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:26,852
- Should we stand here?
- Yeah, in the middle.

227
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:30,940
This is why stocks are terrifying.

228
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,650
I should never play the stock market.

229
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,659
Why did it have to be me?

230
00:11:42,576 --> 00:11:44,286
It had to be someone from the living area.

231
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:45,538
- A player in the living area?
- Yes.

232
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:47,206
- And make them come last?
- Yes.

233
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:49,583
Why is Shindong in last place?

234
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,544
Why did he buy that out of the blue?

235
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:55,172
- Can we have a quick chat?
- Sure.

236
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:00,177
Why did you do that?

237
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:01,721
Was it Won-young's doing?

238
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:02,638
I got played.

239
00:12:02,722 --> 00:12:04,473
- What?
- I got played.

240
00:12:09,019 --> 00:12:10,604
There's no coming back from that?

241
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:12,606
- No, you can't.
- There's no way.

242
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:19,321
<i>I told him I could save him</i>
<i>as long as he didn't place last.</i>

243
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:23,451
But I think this comes down to Shindong
trusting Won-young over me.

244
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,286
That was his mistake.

245
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:29,415
I was the one who pushed for Won-young
to take on the challenge, and he did.

246
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:32,626
<i>So I thought</i>
<i>trust had been built between us,</i>

247
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:35,796
and I figured he would've chosen me
because he trusted me.

248
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,591
I thought, since he believes me,
I'll believe him too,

249
00:12:38,674 --> 00:12:41,594
and we'll survive this together.

250
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:43,888
I just believed everything he said
without questioning it.

251
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:48,476
We all agreed
to Won-young going in there yesterday.

252
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:52,313
If what he laid out is 100% true,

253
00:12:52,396 --> 00:12:53,981
then he probably had no choice either.

254
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,568
Right, I understand. I do, but…

255
00:12:58,235 --> 00:13:00,362
<i>That concludes Round 21.</i>

256
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:03,407
<i>Round 22 will now begin.</i>

257
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:06,619
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

258
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:07,745
- Guys.
- Yes?

259
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:11,707
Let's see if there's a way
to make money using Banger Steel.

260
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:15,294
There is. The alliance token
will go to first place, no matter what.

261
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:18,881
Coax someone high up in the rankings
to buy 500,000 won's worth with it.

262
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:22,468
If they buy in Round 22,
it'll tank to 100 won by Round 23.

263
00:13:22,551 --> 00:13:24,303
- Then we all buy it at 100 won.
- Go all in?

264
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:25,221
Yeah, all in.

265
00:13:25,304 --> 00:13:28,057
It'll still be at 100 won come Round 24.

266
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,643
Then if we get them to sell the 50 shares,

267
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:32,478
it'll go up in the next round.

268
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:36,273
Our candidates for this op are those
who were with us in the living area.

269
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:39,276
Kyung-lyul, Yurisa, and Won-young.

270
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,861
We can't save Shindong.

271
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:43,948
If we're gonna do it,
we need to get on it now.

272
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,491
Otherwise, our plan won't work.

273
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:47,576
Just tell them to buy
right in front of us.

274
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,994
<i>You have one minute left.</i>

275
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:50,037
We need to hurry up.

276
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,164
- We need someone to buy up 50 shares now.
- Who?

277
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:53,791
- Someone reliable.
- How's Kyung-lyul?

278
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:56,293
- Wait, not him. I don't like him!
- Huh?

279
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:00,923
- Kyung-lyul.
- Yes?

280
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:03,717
Hurry.

281
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:05,594
- You okay with Kyung-lyul?
- What?

282
00:14:05,678 --> 00:14:07,012
- Just get on with it.
- Hurry.

283
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:09,306
- We need you to buy… What was it again?
- Steel.

284
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:10,808
Right, buy 50 shares of Steel.

285
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:13,018
- Buy 50 shares of Steel.
- Why? Will you save me then?

286
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:14,270
Yeah, I'll save you.

287
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:15,563
Just buy 50 shares quickly.

288
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:17,690
Wait, I should sell first.

289
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:18,774
Hold on.

290
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:20,359
- I need to sell this first.
- Hurry up.

291
00:14:20,442 --> 00:14:22,361
- I need to make the cash first.
- Right, okay.

292
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:24,613
What was it again? Hold on.

293
00:14:24,697 --> 00:14:26,949
<i>That concludes Round 22.</i>

294
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:28,242
Damn it.

295
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:29,785
New round?

296
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:31,245
- Did you?
- I had no time.

297
00:14:31,328 --> 00:14:33,497
<i>Round 23 will now begin.</i>

298
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:36,333
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

299
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:37,418
BANGER STEEL
▼7,200 WON

300
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:38,335
That didn't work.

301
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,255
- Did we fail?
- Can't we do it now?

302
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:42,172
No.

303
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:44,550
Wait, now I'm screwed.

304
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:46,135
No, you're not screwed.

305
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:49,722
- I just took a hit.
- Hold on a second.

306
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:51,140
I'm off. I can leave, right?

307
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:53,392
Yeah, give us a second.
We need a quick meeting.

308
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:54,310
Okay.

309
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:58,272
- Damn it.
- It was actually a pretty solid strategy.

310
00:14:58,355 --> 00:14:59,607
But now…

311
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,901
Are you trying to
give the first-place player a boost

312
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:04,987
- for the living area token?
- They had me do something, but it failed.

313
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:06,280
I just got screwed over.

314
00:15:06,363 --> 00:15:11,327
So our choice is down to Kyung-lyul,
Yurisa, and Won-young.

315
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:13,913
Won-young's coming back up anyway.
He has that revival item.

316
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:16,415
We don't know if it actually exists,
so let's rule that out.

317
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:18,792
<i>That concludes Round 23.</i>

318
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:21,503
<i>Round 24 will now begin.</i>

319
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:24,423
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

320
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:26,383
It's over now anyway.

321
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:28,218
There's nothing we can do now.

322
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:29,553
Nothing can go up, can it?

323
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,513
I think it's over.

324
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,766
I should've just gone in myself.

325
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:36,936
- This curse is just too much for me.
- The thing is,

326
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:39,813
I supported you
when you volunteered for the challenge.

327
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:42,066
- Right.
- That's why

328
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:45,194
I believed that I could trust you.

329
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:48,489
So when you told me about your plan,
I thought, "Of course, he chose me."

330
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:50,324
"If he trusts me enough,
I'll help him out."

331
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:52,660
That was a major factor.
I just want you to know that.

332
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,163
How do you feel right now?

333
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:20,437
Sorry.

334
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:26,026
<i>That concludes Mystery Stock Market.</i>

335
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,278
<i>Everyone, please gather in the hall.</i>

336
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:32,366
- Taking the center spot?
- Yeah, one last time for a cool shot.

337
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:36,704
<i>Here are the players' asset rankings</i>
<i>by total holdings.</i>

338
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:40,290
<i>Shindong, the lowest-ranked player,</i>

339
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:43,544
<i>is the fifth player</i>
<i>to be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan.

340
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:45,838
<i>Please return your Piece.</i>

341
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,548
Darn, I never got to use my Piece.

342
00:16:47,631 --> 00:16:49,341
<i>I'm sure he was furious.</i>

343
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:53,053
<i>I just straight-up lied to his face</i>
<i>the whole time.</i>

344
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,854
What's wrong with you?

345
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:03,188
Did someone die or something?

346
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:05,607
There's no need to cry so much.

347
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:15,534
<i>Shindong, please leave.</i>

348
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:17,411
Good luck, everyone.

349
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:19,371
- I had a lot of fun.
- Good job.

350
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:22,583
Good luck, Dong-min.

351
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:28,255
I was really looking forward
to playing with you. I'm sorry.

352
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:30,424
- Great work.
- Thank you for everything.

353
00:17:30,507 --> 00:17:31,592
Thank you so much.

354
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:33,010
Let's grab a drink someday.

355
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,636
Why are you crying so much?

356
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:35,596
I just…

357
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,556
You're making me cry.

358
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:38,640
Damn it.

359
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:40,350
<i>He was the first to come to me and say,</i>

360
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:44,688
<i>"I told them in the interview</i>
<i>that I wanted to play with you the most."</i>

361
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:46,315
That made me trust him.

362
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:48,275
<i>We also discovered the secret together.</i>

363
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:53,363
<i>And in the process, I realized</i>
<i>I wanted to keep playing with him.</i>

364
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:54,990
<i>I grew really fond of him.</i>

365
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:58,535
I did trust him rather blindly,

366
00:17:58,619 --> 00:17:59,953
and that's on me.

367
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:03,082
<i>He did what he had to do for himself.</i>

368
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:06,418
<i>I was trying my best too.</i>
<i>I just slipped up in the process.</i>

369
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:08,837
The Shindong you knew before this

370
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:12,216
<i>was an entertainer</i>
<i>performing to make people happy.</i>

371
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:14,384
But here, on <i>The Devil's Plan,</i>

372
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,970
<i>I think I was able to</i>
<i>just be Shin Dong-hee, myself.</i>

373
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:19,389
<i>I was genuinely happy</i>
<i>when things were good,</i>

374
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:21,600
<i>and it made me realize</i>
<i>that I also had my own ambitions.</i>

375
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:25,437
<i>The Devil's Plan</i>
helped me learn about myself.

376
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:26,772
Bye.

377
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:29,483
- Goodbye.
- Great work.

378
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:59,429
THE DEVIL'S PLAN: DEAD AGAIN

379
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:05,769
<i>The following players</i>
<i>have amassed more than 1.5 million won.</i>

380
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:07,104
<i>XITSUH,</i>

381
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:08,480
<i>Oh Hyun-min,</i>

382
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:09,940
<i>Kim Dong-jae,</i>

383
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:11,275
<i>Hyun Kyung-lyul,</i>

384
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,734
<i>and Ha Seok-jin.</i>

385
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:14,611
<i>They will all be rewarded with one Piece.</i>

386
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:17,489
<i>Jang Dong-min has amassed</i>
<i>more than three million won.</i>

387
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:19,700
<i>He will be rewarded with two Pieces.</i>

388
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:23,370
<i>As there are no players who have reached</i>
<i>ten million won in assets,</i>

389
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:26,582
<i>the prize token cannot be obtained.</i>

390
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,835
<i>Based on the rankings,</i>

391
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:34,256
<i>players in first through fourth place</i>
<i>will go to the living area,</i>

392
00:19:34,339 --> 00:19:36,466
<i>and players in fifth through eleventh</i>
<i>will go to prison.</i>

393
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:40,512
<i>Jang Dong-min, the first-place player,</i>
<i>will be rewarded with an advantage,</i>

394
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,264
<i>the alliance token.</i>

395
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:49,646
<i>You may choose one player</i>
<i>heading to prison</i>

396
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,565
<i>and bring them to the living area.</i>

397
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:55,527
<i>Who will you use the alliance token on?</i>

398
00:19:56,945 --> 00:20:00,741
First of all, I wanna thank everyone
for all your hard work today.

399
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:04,369
Looking forward to seeing more
from this player,

400
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:07,372
I'll give this alliance token to…

401
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,836
In this game,

402
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,881
we haven't had much contact
with Yurisa or Kyung-lyul.

403
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:18,050
But if I had to pick,

404
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:20,469
I think we owe Kyung-lyul a bit more.

405
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:23,805
The person we bring over is the person
we'll be working with in tomorrow's game.

406
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,182
- Right.
- Yeah.

407
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:27,726
And it's gonna be even tougher tomorrow.

408
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:29,937
It's time we sent away people
who could be a threat.

409
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:33,440
I'll give this alliance token to…

410
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:36,777
Yurisa.

411
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:49,873
<i>The players for both the living area</i>
<i>and the prison have been decided.</i>

412
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:53,752
<i>Now, please make your way</i>
<i>to your respective living spaces.</i>

413
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:55,379
Have a good sleep tonight.

414
00:20:55,462 --> 00:20:56,797
- Make your way upstairs soon.
- Sure.

415
00:20:58,340 --> 00:20:59,716
- Good job today.
- Congratulations.

416
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,802
- I'm so glad you're coming with us.
- Good job.

417
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:05,639
I can't believe
I'm going up there dressed like this.

418
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:11,311
So you actually meant to end up in prison?

419
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,813
Yeah, why are you here?

420
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:14,398
You didn't say
you'd use the advantage, right?

421
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:16,692
You have to tell them you wanna use it.

422
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:18,026
But I'm sure you knew that.

423
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,445
No, I'm supposed to get a token.

424
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:24,908
<i>There are a few reasons</i>
<i>I didn't use the token.</i>

425
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:26,785
I deceived so many people.

426
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,914
If I had gone up there,

427
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:33,417
I'd be back
where only politicking happens.

428
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:39,131
I wasn't sure if that'd be the right call.
Most of all, I felt guilty about Shindong.

429
00:21:39,214 --> 00:21:41,967
Declaring that I would save myself
at that point felt a bit…

430
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:46,555
I can't exactly put it into words,
but that weighed on me.

431
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:51,435
<i>Players in prison,</i>
<i>please change into the provided outfits.</i>

432
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:55,981
<i>The prison match will begin at 8:30 p.m.</i>

433
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:57,774
Did he say 8:30 p.m.? That's so far away.

434
00:21:57,858 --> 00:21:59,985
- There's nothing to do anyway.
- I know, right?

435
00:22:00,610 --> 00:22:01,486
The clothes are here.

436
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,697
- You can take whatever size you need.
- Thank you.

437
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:06,908
What's upstairs? Is it more spacious?

438
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,827
It's one giant room.

439
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:10,412
You had pig's trotters
for dinner yesterday, right?

440
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:12,164
What about the beds? Are they like these?

441
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:13,457
We're so curious.

442
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:16,209
- Super curious.
- So curious.

443
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:20,589
This is where you guys stayed?

444
00:22:20,672 --> 00:22:22,799
I couldn't wait for you to be up here.

445
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:24,926
What is this?

446
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:26,178
XITSUH.

447
00:22:26,261 --> 00:22:29,890
<i>The floor isn't ice-cold concrete.</i>

448
00:22:29,973 --> 00:22:32,225
<i>It had hardwood floors,</i>
<i>and it was carpeted.</i>

449
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:33,518
<i>It was a different world.</i>

450
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:35,771
I'm finally home.

451
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:41,109
I wanna settle down here
and stay for good.

452
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:43,153
I wanna make one thing clear.

453
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:47,324
The four of us played together
throughout the game today

454
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:50,744
<i>and just picked up one person</i>
<i>from the other team.</i>

455
00:22:50,827 --> 00:22:54,164
But starting tomorrow, it has to be
a full-on five-on-five battle.

456
00:22:54,247 --> 00:22:55,082
I agree.

457
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,667
Starting tomorrow,
there should be no intel sharing.

458
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:58,752
It's do or die.

459
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:01,755
So we have to actually win tomorrow.
Tomorrow is super important.

460
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:04,925
I meant what I said before I chose you.

461
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:07,677
I'm really looking forward to
great things from you.

462
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:08,762
Woof, woof.

463
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:14,476
Honestly, that moved me the most
out of all my survival game experiences.

464
00:23:14,559 --> 00:23:18,063
<i>Since he gave me the token,</i>

465
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:21,191
I plan to work hard
to live up to his trust and faith in me.

466
00:23:21,274 --> 00:23:24,444
Why are you down here, Won-young?

467
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:28,323
You've lied so much
that I can't guess where the truth ends.

468
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:30,117
I was cursed.

469
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,993
Right. The rules seem a bit unclear.

470
00:23:32,619 --> 00:23:35,122
- And that curse…
- What's this curse anyway?

471
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:39,793
There was an opportunity to increase
the prize money by 200 million won,

472
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:42,504
but the barrier was protected by a curse.

473
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:44,339
So what does the curse do?

474
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:46,174
They just call it a curse.

475
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:48,969
"The prize token
is protected by a curse barrier."

476
00:23:49,052 --> 00:23:51,555
- "To break the curse…" I'm cursed.
- So you have no details?

477
00:23:51,638 --> 00:23:53,140
- There's no separate curse.
- He's lying.

478
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:54,850
I've been through this before.

479
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,894
- Still, hear me out.
- He knows what's up.

480
00:23:57,978 --> 00:24:00,063
"If you fail to break the curse,

481
00:24:00,147 --> 00:24:02,691
you will face a severe penalty,
which will bar you from competing

482
00:24:02,774 --> 00:24:03,733
in the finals."

483
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:06,528
<i>He just kept going like he was possessed.</i>

484
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:09,406
"I'm cursed. I've been cursed."

485
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:11,283
We have no idea what this curse is.

486
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:14,286
Hyun-gyu kept asking,
"So what kind of curse is it?"

487
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:16,413
A total heart versus head situation.

488
00:24:16,496 --> 00:24:19,708
And then I was told
that if I broke the curse,

489
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:24,045
I'd be given a token
that would let me move to the living area.

490
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:28,467
But it was called
an ascension token or something.

491
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:30,969
- You should've used it today.
- Yeah.

492
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,596
Why didn't you use it today?

493
00:24:32,679 --> 00:24:34,723
If he had an advantage
that could save him,

494
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:35,807
why didn't he play it?

495
00:24:35,891 --> 00:24:38,894
- He could've just chosen not to use it.
- Considering this,

496
00:24:38,977 --> 00:24:41,563
what he said about the advantage
might not be true.

497
00:24:41,646 --> 00:24:43,648
- You're right.
- I think so too. He might've lied again.

498
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:47,194
Why go out of your way
to raise your odds of elimination today?

499
00:24:47,277 --> 00:24:50,197
And what if you end up going home
after the death room?

500
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:52,157
That's a possibility.

501
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:54,117
- But I wanted to come down here.
- You're confident?

502
00:24:54,201 --> 00:24:55,869
So you're biding your time for later?

503
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,579
Something smells fishy.

504
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,209
Let's just kill him and see.

505
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:05,086
- Yeah, we can check when this airs.
- Sounds good.

506
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:08,215
It'd be funny if he got eliminated.
He'd never get to use that advantage.

507
00:25:08,798 --> 00:25:10,050
"Funny."

508
00:25:11,301 --> 00:25:14,387
Well, Won-young has lied a lot.

509
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:18,391
So if an alliance forms, I think the play
is for everyone but Won-young

510
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,101
to work toward eliminating him.

511
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:23,980
Right now, I see Seok-jin, Hyun-gyu,
and John as potential allies.

512
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:27,692
Anyone outside of those three,
I need to keep an eye on them a bit more.

513
00:25:27,776 --> 00:25:31,905
Kyung-lyul and Won-young
are not really my type of people.

514
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:35,534
They're just not straightforward.

515
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:37,160
They're secretive.

516
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:38,995
Let's play the game.

517
00:25:39,079 --> 00:25:41,581
It's been bugging me
that we never got to finish it.

518
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,336
- Do you have this upstairs too?
- Yes.

519
00:25:46,419 --> 00:25:48,255
- Wall Go II?
- Yeah.

520
00:25:49,005 --> 00:25:51,299
- Have you played it?
- A few rounds.

521
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:52,634
What sucks about being here is that

522
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:55,512
if you practice this in here,
everyone up there knows you are.

523
00:25:55,595 --> 00:25:58,306
They're playing Wall Go II down there.

524
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,433
- I'll take anyone.
- Is it my time to crush you guys?

525
00:26:01,184 --> 00:26:02,227
Rock, paper, scissors.

526
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:03,895
Do I move my counter
and then set up a wall?

527
00:26:03,979 --> 00:26:05,397
- Yes.
- Starting now?

528
00:26:13,363 --> 00:26:16,074
<i>There's something I told myself I'd do</i>
<i>before we began the shoot.</i>

529
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:20,203
I told myself
to inspect the floor carefully

530
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:21,621
if I ended up upstairs.

531
00:26:22,205 --> 00:26:23,456
<i>That's what I did in the living area.</i>

532
00:26:23,540 --> 00:26:25,625
<i>And I told myself to do the opposite</i>
<i>if I ended up downstairs.</i>

533
00:26:25,709 --> 00:26:27,085
<i>Since I'm in prison now,</i>

534
00:26:27,168 --> 00:26:29,212
<i>I've been inspecting the ceiling.</i>

535
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,597
- He's unbelievable.
- You're kidding me.

536
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,057
Won-young's quite a character.

537
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,434
Did you inspect it all already?

538
00:26:42,517 --> 00:26:44,686
- Not that thoroughly.
- We didn't go that far.

539
00:26:49,024 --> 00:26:52,485
When he was going around
smashing everything, I was like,

540
00:26:52,569 --> 00:26:53,987
"Hold on. Maybe that's a ladder."

541
00:26:54,821 --> 00:26:58,867
I think it reflects
my desire to get upstairs.

542
00:26:58,950 --> 00:27:00,827
I'm really gonna try climbing this thing.

543
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:02,912
Here I go.

544
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:06,625
There's nothing you can do,
even if you get up there.

545
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:12,255
This can't be something, right?

546
00:27:14,716 --> 00:27:16,468
Is there really nothing down here?

547
00:27:16,551 --> 00:27:18,637
Must we continue
making a fool of ourselves?

548
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,472
I don't see anything.

549
00:27:21,431 --> 00:27:23,391
When there's nothing to eat,

550
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:26,478
the last thing you want
is to waste energy on nonsense.

551
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:30,106
Is there really nothing down here?

552
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:32,651
There's absolutely nothing here.

553
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:35,153
I'm exhausted.

554
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:41,076
Food has arrived. Must be nice.

555
00:27:41,785 --> 00:27:43,161
Guess it's dinnertime.

556
00:27:43,244 --> 00:27:45,538
- Wow. Dinnertime.
- Our food is here.

557
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:48,041
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

558
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:49,918
Braised chicken, seaweed soup.
Any birthdays today?

559
00:27:50,001 --> 00:27:51,127
I was reborn today.

560
00:27:51,836 --> 00:27:53,213
I'm a new man today.

561
00:27:58,843 --> 00:28:01,429
This is insanely good.

562
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:03,431
Our dinner is here too.

563
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:07,852
If you don't finish your bread,
you have to wrap it up.

564
00:28:07,936 --> 00:28:10,772
If not, it'll be gone
after the prison match.

565
00:28:10,855 --> 00:28:12,440
I need to eat something right now.

566
00:28:12,524 --> 00:28:13,566
Help yourself.

567
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:15,026
It's warm.

568
00:28:16,861 --> 00:28:18,488
But you know,

569
00:28:18,571 --> 00:28:20,073
I think this suits me better.

570
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:28,081
Isn't this bread better than yesterday's?

571
00:28:28,164 --> 00:28:30,333
- It's much better.
- Way softer.

572
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,421
There are olives too. It doesn't get
stuck in your teeth as much.

573
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:37,674
Yesterday's was terrible, wasn't it?

574
00:28:37,757 --> 00:28:39,801
Even just getting a good meal

575
00:28:39,884 --> 00:28:41,469
- It makes a difference.
- is a big win.

576
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:42,387
Absolutely.

577
00:28:42,470 --> 00:28:43,930
Let's keep this going, Dong-min.

578
00:28:44,013 --> 00:28:44,848
I'll do my best.

579
00:28:44,931 --> 00:28:46,349
- I've been number two for a long time.
- Right.

580
00:28:46,433 --> 00:28:47,308
And it's not bad.

581
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:52,188
I think I'd be fine
with being joint number three.

582
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:54,190
By the way, who's the leader down there?

583
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:55,400
There isn't one.

584
00:28:55,483 --> 00:28:57,402
- There's no unifying force.
- None.

585
00:28:57,485 --> 00:28:59,821
I mean, think about yesterday.

586
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,031
Sure, the prison match was coming up,

587
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:05,535
but not a single person stepped up to say,
"Hey, why don't we try this?"

588
00:29:05,618 --> 00:29:10,373
There are far too many players
with a lone wolf mindset down there.

589
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:14,169
Seok-jin is a former champion
and an excellent player.

590
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,504
- There are so many great players there.
- Hyun-gyu's a former champion too.

591
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:18,798
- But they're all the same.
- They all wanna play alone.

592
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:22,010
They'll be out for blood tomorrow,

593
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:24,137
not because of any animosity toward us,

594
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:26,139
but out of resentment
over their helplessness.

595
00:29:26,222 --> 00:29:27,390
Right, they'll wanna win.

596
00:29:27,474 --> 00:29:31,269
They're not used to losing so helplessly.

597
00:29:31,352 --> 00:29:34,272
The fact that they've been
so helpless and powerless

598
00:29:34,355 --> 00:29:35,315
must be infuriating.

599
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:39,360
I really wanna make
at least one proper play before I go.

600
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:42,238
Even with the majority,
we just keep getting wrecked.

601
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:45,492
We keep getting crushed
because no one's in control.

602
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:47,368
It did seem like
a lot of information leaked out.

603
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:49,579
- You're right.
- But the thing is, there were players

604
00:29:49,662 --> 00:29:51,080
from the living area on the team.

605
00:29:51,164 --> 00:29:53,875
Shindong, Yurisa, and I already had a deal

606
00:29:53,958 --> 00:29:56,085
to work with the players
from the living area.

607
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:57,462
- So wavering was inevitable.
- Right.

608
00:29:57,545 --> 00:30:01,299
Whether there was information
leaking or not,

609
00:30:01,382 --> 00:30:04,886
<i>seeing our teammates</i>
<i>have such open communication with them</i>

610
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:07,138
<i>- had an impact on everyone.</i>
<i>- Right.</i>

611
00:30:07,222 --> 00:30:11,351
Once people start wondering
why they're even playing with that person,

612
00:30:11,434 --> 00:30:13,812
they start going solo.

613
00:30:13,895 --> 00:30:15,271
Let's play five-on-five tomorrow.

614
00:30:16,731 --> 00:30:18,316
We have to do that at least once.

615
00:30:18,983 --> 00:30:20,777
Tomorrow, I wanna do things properly too.

616
00:30:20,860 --> 00:30:22,403
I think I had it wrong.

617
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:24,405
I was just trying to survive.

618
00:30:25,698 --> 00:30:26,533
I need to win.

619
00:30:26,616 --> 00:30:28,868
Just surviving day after day
seems a bit meaningless.

620
00:30:28,952 --> 00:30:31,538
If we can't break through here,
we'll never win.

621
00:30:31,621 --> 00:30:32,997
- Right.
- In the end.

622
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:37,293
If Kyung-lyul manages to survive today,

623
00:30:38,044 --> 00:30:39,295
he'll come back with vengeance.

624
00:30:39,379 --> 00:30:40,255
Right.

625
00:30:40,338 --> 00:30:42,382
As for Won-young,

626
00:30:42,465 --> 00:30:47,345
he kind of took himself
out of the picture on his own.

627
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:50,932
Kyung-lyul was the only one
from the living area yesterday

628
00:30:51,015 --> 00:30:52,517
who didn't make it back here.

629
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:55,144
We also had him do that thing.

630
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:57,355
- Buy 50 shares of Steel.
- Why? Will you save me then?

631
00:30:57,438 --> 00:30:58,606
Yeah, I'll save you.

632
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:01,484
If he's thinking we only abandoned him,

633
00:31:01,568 --> 00:31:05,363
- he could really have it out for us.
- He must be furious.

634
00:31:06,114 --> 00:31:08,241
If we don't take down Dong-min,
we'll be here for the week.

635
00:31:08,324 --> 00:31:10,410
Let's at least make a dent.

636
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:15,331
If anything, I think this prison uniform
actually suits me better.

637
00:31:15,415 --> 00:31:17,542
What can I do?

638
00:31:18,626 --> 00:31:20,044
Let's band together.

639
00:31:20,128 --> 00:31:23,298
Why don't we start
by sharing our childhood stories?

640
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:24,799
Our childhood?

641
00:31:30,513 --> 00:31:31,389
They sound happy.

642
00:31:32,599 --> 00:31:33,433
How nice.

643
00:31:33,516 --> 00:31:38,354
- So, Won-young, you're also a father?
- Yes, my kid just turned one.

644
00:31:38,438 --> 00:31:40,064
- Just one? How cute.
- They just turned one.

645
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:43,818
Hopefully, if our kids
ever see this in the future,

646
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:45,737
they'll think,
"What an honest man my father is."

647
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:48,114
Right, not someone shady.

648
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:49,991
"My dad's not lousy."

649
00:31:50,074 --> 00:31:51,659
But there's already some footage.

650
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:03,087
How did Eun-yu survive
6 days in here in Season 2?

651
00:32:03,171 --> 00:32:04,213
She's amazing.

652
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:05,173
Seriously.

653
00:32:05,256 --> 00:32:06,799
- So amazing.
- Six days in here?

654
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:09,302
I don't think I could.

655
00:32:09,385 --> 00:32:11,095
It's not just the discomfort.

656
00:32:11,179 --> 00:32:13,765
- It's having to wonder every night
- Right.

657
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:15,683
- whether tonight's the night you go home.
- Yeah, exactly.

658
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:18,311
I feel like someone will do the same
this season too.

659
00:32:19,520 --> 00:32:22,482
- One of you two might stay for the week.
- Yeah, I can see that.

660
00:32:23,691 --> 00:32:25,234
Oh yes. Finally.

661
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:30,239
<i>The prison match will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

662
00:32:30,323 --> 00:32:31,366
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

663
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:32,742
<i>In today's prison match,</i>

664
00:32:32,825 --> 00:32:36,245
<i>two players will be eliminated</i>
<i>and leave </i>The Devil's Plan.

665
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:37,914
- What?
- Two again?

666
00:32:37,997 --> 00:32:40,124
- Why?
- What's with all these eliminations?

667
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:42,502
We'll be at the finale in two days
at this rate.

668
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:46,547
<i>Now, let me introduce</i>
<i>the second prison match.</i>

669
00:32:46,631 --> 00:32:48,549
<i>Today's prison match is</i>

670
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:51,177
<i>- Russian Roulette.</i>
- Russian Roulette?

671
00:32:51,260 --> 00:32:55,431
<i>In Russian Roulette,</i>
<i>players will track the bullets</i>

672
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:57,934
<i>to avoid them</i>
<i>in the firing stage at the end.</i>

673
00:32:58,017 --> 00:33:00,103
<i>Players will begin the game</i>

674
00:33:00,186 --> 00:33:04,607
<i>with a personal device</i>
<i>and 16 virtual credits.</i>

675
00:33:05,191 --> 00:33:07,402
<i>Players will draw a lottery ball</i>

676
00:33:07,485 --> 00:33:11,155
<i>and be assigned to one of six positions.</i>

677
00:33:11,239 --> 00:33:14,283
<i>The player who draws one</i>
<i>becomes the first player,</i>

678
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:18,579
<i>and the first player's role</i>
<i>rotates clockwise each round.</i>

679
00:33:19,956 --> 00:33:24,252
<i>The gun used in Russian Roulette</i>
<i>has six chambers,</i>

680
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:28,089
<i>two of which are randomly loaded</i>
<i>with bullets.</i>

681
00:33:29,549 --> 00:33:30,758
This is gonna be fun.

682
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:34,721
<i>On their turn,</i>
<i>each player will use their device</i>

683
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:37,807
<i>to select one</i>
<i>of the following five actions.</i>

684
00:33:38,433 --> 00:33:42,061
<i>Public investigation costs one credit.</i>

685
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:44,897
<i>With it, players can select</i>
<i>two adjacent chambers</i>

686
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:48,151
<i>to check for bullets publicly.</i>

687
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:49,318
Publicly?

688
00:33:50,778 --> 00:33:54,198
<i>Private investigation costs two credits.</i>

689
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:57,201
<i>With it, players can select</i>
<i>two adjacent chambers for inspection</i>

690
00:33:57,285 --> 00:34:01,289
<i>and receive the results privately</i>
<i>on their device.</i>

691
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:05,668
<i>Single rotate costs three credits.</i>

692
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:09,172
<i>With it, players can rotate the gun</i>
<i>one position clockwise.</i>

693
00:34:09,797 --> 00:34:12,967
<i>Double rotate costs four credits.</i>

694
00:34:13,051 --> 00:34:16,304
<i>With it, players can rotate the gun</i>
<i>two positions clockwise,</i>

695
00:34:16,387 --> 00:34:19,766
<i>and the rotation results</i>
<i>are revealed to all players.</i>

696
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:24,228
<i>Manipulate costs six credits.</i>

697
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:28,900
<i>With it, players can privately swap</i>
<i>the states of two adjacent chambers.</i>

698
00:34:29,609 --> 00:34:35,156
<i>Players cannot load</i>
<i>all six required credits at once.</i>

699
00:34:35,239 --> 00:34:38,284
<i>A maximum of three credits</i>
<i>may be submitted at a time,</i>

700
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:40,661
<i>and submitted credits accumulate.</i>

701
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:42,705
They'll need two turns, then.

702
00:34:42,789 --> 00:34:45,291
<i>The player whose submitted credits</i>

703
00:34:45,374 --> 00:34:50,088
<i>complete the total of six</i>
<i>performs the manipulate privately.</i>

704
00:34:50,171 --> 00:34:53,424
<i>If the submitted credits exceed six,</i>

705
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:56,594
<i>the remaining credits are forfeited,</i>
<i>and the count resets.</i>

706
00:34:58,054 --> 00:34:59,430
Forfeited and reset?

707
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:02,767
<i>In the process,</i>

708
00:35:02,850 --> 00:35:06,395
<i>if one of the two selected chambers</i>
<i>contains a bullet,</i>

709
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,314
<i>the bullet's position changes.</i>

710
00:35:08,397 --> 00:35:09,398
This is insane.

711
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:14,862
<i>If both chambers contain a bullet</i>
<i>or are empty, nothing changes.</i>

712
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:19,534
<i>Only the player themselves</i>
<i>can see their remaining credit count.</i>

713
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:22,787
<i>A player who has used all their credits</i>

714
00:35:22,870 --> 00:35:26,499
<i>will automatically pass on their turn,</i>

715
00:35:26,582 --> 00:35:30,336
<i>and this pass is also announced</i>
<i>as a private action.</i>

716
00:35:31,504 --> 00:35:33,631
<i>Rounds continue in the same manner.</i>

717
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:38,427
<i>The moment three out of six players</i>
<i>have exhausted all their credits,</i>

718
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:40,054
<i>firing begins.</i>

719
00:35:40,596 --> 00:35:41,764
Then the trigger is pulled?

720
00:35:43,182 --> 00:35:46,727
<i>Firing starts with the player</i>
<i>the gun is pointing at</i>

721
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:48,688
<i>and continues clockwise.</i>

722
00:35:49,355 --> 00:35:52,191
<i>The two players standing in the positions</i>
<i>with loaded chambers</i>

723
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:54,277
<i>will be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan,

724
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:57,864
<i>and the surviving players</i>
<i>will receive one Piece each.</i>

725
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:02,368
<i>The game will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

726
00:36:02,451 --> 00:36:05,288
So this is a one-off match
with a single firing phase?

727
00:36:05,371 --> 00:36:07,290
This is brutal for six people.

728
00:36:09,375 --> 00:36:13,713
- A one in three chance of elimination.
- This is basically just sheer luck.

729
00:36:15,089 --> 00:36:16,257
Positioning is gonna be key.

730
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:19,510
Right, and the players next to you.

731
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:21,012
Because you can check
your chamber and theirs?

732
00:36:21,095 --> 00:36:23,723
If you ally with the person next to you,

733
00:36:23,806 --> 00:36:26,184
you can manipulate in one go
by adding three credits each.

734
00:36:26,267 --> 00:36:28,352
So two players contribute together?

735
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:31,981
If both of us are almost out of credits
and the bullets are on the other side,

736
00:36:32,064 --> 00:36:34,609
we can go for manipulate,
empty our pockets, and trigger the firing.

737
00:36:34,692 --> 00:36:37,945
And at least between the two,
they'd have full transparency

738
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:40,198
on how many credits each other has left.

739
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:42,909
Right, and it'll be over quickly.

740
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:44,744
I'll have a better idea after the lottery.

741
00:36:44,827 --> 00:36:45,661
True.

742
00:36:45,745 --> 00:36:49,624
If four players band together,
they can easily send two people home.

743
00:36:49,707 --> 00:36:51,209
- Absolutely.
- Yeah.

744
00:36:51,709 --> 00:36:54,921
You'd know how much credit is left.

745
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:57,590
- It's best to conserve credits.
- Especially early on.

746
00:36:57,673 --> 00:36:59,258
You need to build a group of three

747
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:02,136
with the people next to you
to complete the manipulate quickly.

748
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:06,140
I think once they're in there,
they could get desperate enough to do it,

749
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:09,185
but before they are,
I don't think they'd form alliances.

750
00:37:09,268 --> 00:37:11,604
I was with the majority of them yesterday.

751
00:37:11,687 --> 00:37:14,815
The conditions aren't right for that,
and there's no one to spearhead it.

752
00:37:14,899 --> 00:37:16,234
Should we just go for solo play?

753
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:18,611
Then it'll be all luck.

754
00:37:18,694 --> 00:37:20,738
Groups of two seem ideal.

755
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:24,492
Or should we just
go for a four-on-two game?

756
00:37:24,575 --> 00:37:26,744
- Four-on-two?
- That'd be ideal.

757
00:37:28,037 --> 00:37:30,206
We might as well
if we're not gonna play solo.

758
00:37:30,289 --> 00:37:33,000
We just happen to have
two new players anyway.

759
00:37:33,542 --> 00:37:34,961
Our hands are tied.

760
00:37:35,044 --> 00:37:36,879
With the way things are going,
that's true.

761
00:37:36,963 --> 00:37:39,507
I realized it was a politics game
when the rules were announced.

762
00:37:39,590 --> 00:37:41,926
There were
the four original prison members

763
00:37:42,009 --> 00:37:43,386
<i>and the newbies, Won-young and me.</i>

764
00:37:43,469 --> 00:37:45,596
<i>The goal was to kill two, not one.</i>

765
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:47,139
Are we really playing four-on-two?

766
00:37:47,223 --> 00:37:50,476
I mean, why not?
They're doing it upstairs.

767
00:37:50,559 --> 00:37:52,520
They already do it in the main match.

768
00:37:52,603 --> 00:37:55,523
- But the main match involves a lot more.
- Right.

769
00:37:55,606 --> 00:37:58,734
<i>Ultimately, you have to organize</i>
<i>into groups and gang up,</i>

770
00:37:58,818 --> 00:38:00,987
<i>and that's not really something</i>
<i>I like doing.</i>

771
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:02,989
<i>I thought about it a lot.</i>

772
00:38:03,072 --> 00:38:06,575
Going with the four-on-two plan
is a guaranteed win,

773
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,411
and that's the whole idea
behind <i>The Devil's Plan.</i>

774
00:38:08,494 --> 00:38:12,373
<i>Besides, we don't know</i>
<i>when those two will turn on us.</i>

775
00:38:12,456 --> 00:38:13,582
So this is how…

776
00:38:13,666 --> 00:38:16,168
We're not saying
we'll be targeting you two, per se.

777
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:17,920
But we'll make the necessary decisions…

778
00:38:18,004 --> 00:38:19,380
- Depending on the situation.
- Exactly.

779
00:38:19,463 --> 00:38:21,382
Right, we've got to if we wanna survive.

780
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:25,261
Can you just spare me?

781
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:28,639
You know we're joking, right?

782
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:31,183
It's hard to tell where the joke stops.

783
00:38:31,267 --> 00:38:34,478
None of us
can guarantee anything right now.

784
00:38:34,562 --> 00:38:36,147
Once we get our spots,

785
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:39,483
we'll naturally be drawn to one of
the two people on either side of us.

786
00:38:40,818 --> 00:38:42,111
Here we go.

787
00:38:42,194 --> 00:38:44,613
<i>The prison match will begin shortly.</i>

788
00:38:45,156 --> 00:38:46,824
<i>All players in prison,</i>

789
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:51,287
<i>please make your way to the death room</i>
<i>with your Pieces.</i>

790
00:38:51,370 --> 00:38:54,623
That gong sound
hits you right in the chest.

791
00:38:55,458 --> 00:38:56,876
- Let's have a fun game.
- Let's go.

792
00:38:57,960 --> 00:38:59,754
I don't remember
coming back this way yesterday.

793
00:39:01,047 --> 00:39:02,798
We're dead men walking.

794
00:39:03,299 --> 00:39:05,760
It'd be easier for us
if the people with more Pieces

795
00:39:05,843 --> 00:39:07,219
- got eliminated.
- That's true.

796
00:39:09,138 --> 00:39:10,264
Hello.

797
00:39:19,273 --> 00:39:21,776
What's with these scary handcuffs here?

798
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:22,693
It's Russian Roulette.

799
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,862
They usually tie you up
during Russian Roulette.

800
00:39:24,945 --> 00:39:26,364
- Yeah.
- So you can't run away.

801
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:32,620
I guess they're gonna cuff just one hand
to keep you from moving.

802
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:33,621
That's cruel.

803
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:38,125
<i>We will now begin the second prison match,</i>
<i>Russian Roulette.</i>

804
