I have eight credits left.

1182
01:00:55,401 --> 01:00:57,654
He doesn't know about C,

1183
01:00:57,737 --> 01:00:59,030
and he has eight credits left.

1184
01:01:08,081 --> 01:01:09,457
This is the final selection.

1185
01:01:10,541 --> 01:01:14,420
There's a good chance we'll get to firing
after this round.

1186
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:18,132
Considering all the manipulations,
we might not have a lot of credits left.

1187
01:01:28,142 --> 01:01:31,312
I'll add three to A and F.
Do you wanna put in three as well?

1188
01:01:31,396 --> 01:01:32,772
There isn't one in B.

1189
01:01:37,777 --> 01:01:40,613
<i>At that point, I knew there was a bullet</i>
<i>in the chamber in front of me.</i>

1190
01:01:40,697 --> 01:01:43,032
John had exactly three credits left,

1191
01:01:43,116 --> 01:01:44,784
and I still had a lot left.

1192
01:01:44,867 --> 01:01:47,620
So even though I felt bad for JAE JAE,
I suggested we let her go.

1193
01:01:50,456 --> 01:01:51,416
Hold on.

1194
01:01:52,333 --> 01:01:54,544
If one ends up in F,

1195
01:01:55,962 --> 01:01:58,423
then the other one
will be in C or D, right?

1196
01:02:04,971 --> 01:02:06,139
You think it'll end here?

1197
01:02:07,014 --> 01:02:07,890
Okay.

1198
01:02:10,351 --> 01:02:11,602
MANIPULATE

1199
01:02:11,686 --> 01:02:13,563
3 CREDITS
SUBMIT

1200
01:02:21,529 --> 01:02:22,363
SELECTION COMPLETE

1201
01:02:22,447 --> 01:02:23,740
MANIPULATE SUCCESSFUL!
CHAMBER SWAP COMPLETE

1202
01:02:23,823 --> 01:02:26,159
Jeong Hyun-gyu's private action
has been completed.

1203
01:02:26,951 --> 01:02:29,078
John Park, please choose an action.

1204
01:02:32,206 --> 01:02:33,583
I'm leaving it up to fate now.

1205
01:02:33,666 --> 01:02:34,625
God help me.

1206
01:02:37,420 --> 01:02:38,838
3 CREDITS
SUBMIT

1207
01:02:38,921 --> 01:02:40,131
MANIPULATE UNAVAILABLE
CREDITS HAVE BEEN ACCUMULATED

1208
01:02:40,214 --> 01:02:42,467
John Park's private action
has been completed.

1209
01:02:43,050 --> 01:02:45,553
Ha Seok-jin, please choose an action.

1210
01:02:47,346 --> 01:02:48,181
Hold on.

1211
01:02:50,683 --> 01:02:51,684
Did you swap them?

1212
01:02:52,810 --> 01:02:53,770
I did.

1213
01:02:55,271 --> 01:02:56,981
- You're out of credits, right?
- Yeah.

1214
01:02:57,064 --> 01:02:58,274
Can't we just say it outright?

1215
01:02:58,357 --> 01:03:01,652
Do I have to stay in the dark
until the gun suddenly goes off?

1216
01:03:03,821 --> 01:03:06,365
- I'll just tell you what I know.
- Okay.

1217
01:03:08,159 --> 01:03:09,327
There's one bullet in F,

1218
01:03:09,410 --> 01:03:12,079
- and I've used up all my credits.
- Okay.

1219
01:03:17,084 --> 01:03:20,713
Can you at least give us
a gist of what's going on?

1220
01:03:20,797 --> 01:03:23,216
You know, it's just…

1221
01:03:23,299 --> 01:03:24,300
PRIVATE INVESTIGATION

1222
01:03:24,383 --> 01:03:25,593
We don't know either.

1223
01:03:25,676 --> 01:03:26,511
SELECTION COMPLETE

1224
01:03:26,594 --> 01:03:27,929
PRIVATE INVESTIGATION RESULTS
JOHN PARK, HA SEOK-JIN

1225
01:03:28,012 --> 01:03:32,475
B, JOHN PARK: X
C, HA SEOK-JIN: O

1226
01:03:32,558 --> 01:03:35,019
Ha Seok-jin's private action
has been completed.

1227
01:03:43,110 --> 01:03:45,238
Jung Won-young, please choose an action.

1228
01:03:50,117 --> 01:03:52,787
Are John and Seok-jin both out of credits?

1229
01:03:56,165 --> 01:03:57,625
Just one of them.

1230
01:04:00,753 --> 01:04:03,256
<i>The last time I checked,</i>
<i>the bullets were in chambers A and C.</i>

1231
01:04:03,339 --> 01:04:06,342
Jung Won-young's private action
has been completed.

1232
01:04:06,425 --> 01:04:09,262
I just decided to make my decision
based on the most recent info.

1233
01:04:09,345 --> 01:04:12,557
I first assumed that the bullets
were in chambers A and C.

1234
01:04:12,640 --> 01:04:14,725
Since there's a chamber in between them,

1235
01:04:14,809 --> 01:04:16,811
you get a triangle across the players.

1236
01:04:16,894 --> 01:04:18,813
I wanted to set it up

1237
01:04:18,896 --> 01:04:22,191
so I could double rotate
with me in between.

1238
01:04:22,275 --> 01:04:23,651
JUNG WON-YOUNG
SELECT ACTION

1239
01:04:23,734 --> 01:04:25,820
DOUBLE ROTATE

1240
01:04:27,280 --> 01:04:30,116
Jung Won-young has chosen double rotate.

1241
01:04:38,082 --> 01:04:39,917
The gun has been rotated twice.

1242
01:04:41,085 --> 01:04:42,962
You really saved up those credits.

1243
01:04:43,045 --> 01:04:44,922
There shouldn't be any left.

1244
01:04:45,006 --> 01:04:46,674
A double rotate costs four credits.

1245
01:04:49,468 --> 01:04:51,220
Next, Hyun Kyung-lyul.

1246
01:04:51,304 --> 01:04:52,722
Please choose an action.

1247
01:04:59,937 --> 01:05:01,564
Did you do that knowing where they are?

1248
01:05:05,109 --> 01:05:08,571
It's gonna fire soon,
so this might change…

1249
01:05:10,072 --> 01:05:13,784
I used up my credits
because I wanted to trigger the firing.

1250
01:05:25,546 --> 01:05:28,382
This must really feel like
real Russian Roulette for Kyung-lyul.

1251
01:05:28,466 --> 01:05:32,011
It's all about rotating the gun now.

1252
01:05:34,388 --> 01:05:37,099
- Does anybody wanna tell me anything?
- What?

1253
01:05:38,017 --> 01:05:43,814
Those who'll die if I choose rotate
and trigger firing must know who they are.

1254
01:05:46,067 --> 01:05:47,944
Anybody wanna say anything?

1255
01:05:48,027 --> 01:05:50,237
Are you sure it'll trigger a firing?

1256
01:05:50,321 --> 01:05:52,281
There's a chance it might not,

1257
01:05:52,365 --> 01:05:54,700
but I think I can control that.

1258
01:05:55,326 --> 01:05:58,496
I guess he's saying he's gonna
do something that could make it go off.

1259
01:06:02,375 --> 01:06:04,710
<i>I had four credits left,</i>

1260
01:06:04,794 --> 01:06:08,172
<i>so I could either</i>
<i>rotate once and continue</i>

1261
01:06:08,255 --> 01:06:09,757
<i>or rotate twice.</i>

1262
01:06:09,840 --> 01:06:15,471
My gut was telling me
there was a bullet in my chamber.

1263
01:06:15,554 --> 01:06:18,265
<i>I could evade it with a single rotate.</i>

1264
01:06:18,349 --> 01:06:22,812
<i>But if JAE JAE also did the same,</i>
<i>it might end up back in front of me.</i>

1265
01:06:27,692 --> 01:06:28,526
Whatever.

1266
01:06:28,609 --> 01:06:29,610
Hyun Kyung-lyul…

1267
01:06:34,281 --> 01:06:36,033
has chosen single rotate.

1268
01:06:36,117 --> 01:06:37,034
Single?

1269
01:06:39,120 --> 01:06:39,954
Single?

1270
01:06:41,372 --> 01:06:42,790
The gun has been rotated once.

1271
01:06:47,169 --> 01:06:49,588
- JAE JAE, please choose an action.
- Right.

1272
01:06:49,672 --> 01:06:52,883
<i>I only had one credit left,</i>
<i>so my last hope was to manipulate.</i>

1273
01:06:58,723 --> 01:07:01,225
JAE JAE's private action
has been completed.

1274
01:07:01,308 --> 01:07:02,810
The firing will happen soon.

1275
01:07:03,644 --> 01:07:06,230
<i>Three players</i>
<i>have exhausted all their credits.</i>

1276
01:07:06,313 --> 01:07:08,357
<i>Firing will now begin.</i>

1277
01:07:10,109 --> 01:07:10,943
Oh jeez.

1278
01:07:11,027 --> 01:07:12,028
Huh?

1279
01:07:13,320 --> 01:07:14,155
Oh jeez.

1280
01:07:14,864 --> 01:07:16,532
JUNG WON-YOUNG: SAFE

1281
01:07:16,615 --> 01:07:17,867
He survived.

1282
01:07:22,538 --> 01:07:23,873
HYUN KYUNG-LYUL: SAFE

1283
01:07:23,956 --> 01:07:25,249
We both survived?

1284
01:07:29,879 --> 01:07:31,088
Is it me?

1285
01:07:31,172 --> 01:07:33,049
- It's JAE JAE.
- Damn.

1286
01:07:33,132 --> 01:07:34,383
That's nuts.

1287
01:07:34,467 --> 01:07:36,510
If he hadn't rotated it, then…

1288
01:07:43,142 --> 01:07:49,315
JEONG HYUN-GYU: SAFE

1289
01:07:49,398 --> 01:07:51,067
JOHN PARK: SAFE

1290
01:07:51,150 --> 01:07:52,401
- It's Seok-jin?
- It's Seok-jin.

1291
01:08:00,951 --> 01:08:01,869
Damn.

1292
01:08:02,870 --> 01:08:03,996
So that's how things were.

1293
01:08:08,042 --> 01:08:10,127
<i>JAE JAE and Ha Seok-jin</i>

1294
01:08:10,211 --> 01:08:14,298
<i>are the sixth and seventh players</i>
<i>to be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan.

1295
01:08:14,965 --> 01:08:16,634
<i>Please return your Pieces.</i>

1296
01:08:16,717 --> 01:08:19,178
I can't believe
I'm losing all these Pieces.

1297
01:08:21,514 --> 01:08:23,808
I never even got to play with Seok-jin.

1298
01:08:24,767 --> 01:08:28,771
Alliances aren't all that bad.

1299
01:08:28,854 --> 01:08:30,481
Your survival is on the line.

1300
01:08:31,732 --> 01:08:33,150
- You got this.
- Good job.

1301
01:08:33,234 --> 01:08:35,778
- Good luck.
- I'll give it my all.

1302
01:08:35,861 --> 01:08:37,822
- Make sure to leave a dent, okay?
- Good job.

1303
01:08:37,905 --> 01:08:39,615
- Bye, Seok-jin.
- Take care.

1304
01:08:39,698 --> 01:08:41,200
- See you out there.
- Bye.

1305
01:08:42,493 --> 01:08:44,286
<i>I remember when I first got the call.</i>

1306
01:08:44,370 --> 01:08:46,831
I wondered if an opportunity like this
would ever come around again

1307
01:08:46,914 --> 01:08:49,416
<i>at my age and at this time in my life.</i>

1308
01:08:49,500 --> 01:08:50,751
<i>I knew it'd be embarrassing</i>

1309
01:08:51,335 --> 01:08:52,920
<i>and difficult,</i>

1310
01:08:53,629 --> 01:08:55,548
but given the chance,

1311
01:08:55,631 --> 01:08:57,258
I'd do it all over again.

1312
01:08:58,092 --> 01:09:00,803
Even if I had known this was a tournament
of champions, I would've come.

1313
01:09:00,886 --> 01:09:04,557
This show rekindled
the competitive drive and fighting spirit

1314
01:09:04,640 --> 01:09:06,267
I had lost somewhere along the way.

1315
01:09:06,350 --> 01:09:09,103
<i>It also brought</i>
<i>many new people into my life.</i>

1316
01:09:09,186 --> 01:09:11,814
<i>I've been really grateful</i>
<i>for the franchise itself.</i>

1317
01:09:11,897 --> 01:09:15,651
Before this prison match started,
the six of us were talking

1318
01:09:15,734 --> 01:09:19,738
<i>about leaving a dent in the alliance</i>
<i>of the players in the living area,</i>

1319
01:09:19,822 --> 01:09:23,409
<i>and they asked me to step up</i>
<i>and become a leader.</i>

1320
01:09:28,038 --> 01:09:29,290
Too bad I'll never get to.

1321
01:09:29,373 --> 01:09:31,917
<i>- Good job, everyone.</i>
<i>- Good job.</i>

1322
01:09:32,001 --> 01:09:33,377
<i>Good job.</i>

1323
01:09:33,460 --> 01:09:34,795
<i>- Were you waiting for me?</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

1324
01:09:34,879 --> 01:09:36,297
<i>- We have to leave together.</i>
<i>- Really?</i>

1325
01:09:36,380 --> 01:09:37,798
<i>I guess there's a goodbye shot.</i>

1326
01:09:46,348 --> 01:09:47,349
Let's go.

1327
01:09:47,433 --> 01:09:49,602
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1328
01:09:50,519 --> 01:09:51,353
- Hold on.
- What is this?

1329
01:10:09,705 --> 01:10:11,916
Who would refuse to go to the exile zone?

1330
01:10:11,999 --> 01:10:13,417
I know, right?

1331
01:10:21,175 --> 01:10:22,009
Damn it.

1332
01:10:22,092 --> 01:10:23,552
OPENING THE RED DOOR
WILL TAKE YOU TO THE EXILE ZONE,

1333
01:10:23,636 --> 01:10:24,887
WHERE YOU'LL BE GIVEN ANOTHER CHANCE
TO RETURN TO THE GAME

1334
01:10:24,970 --> 01:10:26,263
Go into exile, huh?

1335
01:10:26,347 --> 01:10:28,307
Where is this exile zone anyway?

1336
01:10:28,390 --> 01:10:29,558
We need to check it out.

1337
01:10:29,642 --> 01:10:31,393
- We need to see what it is.
- It's so fishy.

1338
01:10:31,477 --> 01:10:32,311
Right.

1339
01:10:46,158 --> 01:10:47,534
This is insane.

1340
01:10:47,618 --> 01:10:49,370
- It's a bit scary.
- Right?

1341
01:10:49,453 --> 01:10:51,413
- It's creepy.
- Yeah.

1342
01:10:53,040 --> 01:10:54,708
I wonder where this will lead to.

1343
01:10:54,792 --> 01:10:57,169
Does this mean no one who's gone
to the exile zone so far has made it back?

1344
01:10:57,253 --> 01:10:58,379
The corridor goes on forever.

1345
01:11:00,130 --> 01:11:02,383
They won't give us anything here.

1346
01:11:02,466 --> 01:11:04,551
But there will be another game, right?

1347
01:11:05,594 --> 01:11:08,180
Why did they build all these mazes?

1348
01:11:08,264 --> 01:11:10,057
Maybe I should've just gone home.

1349
01:11:10,140 --> 01:11:13,727
This is my first survival program,
and it's just so…

1350
01:11:13,811 --> 01:11:15,229
The worst welcome ever.

1351
01:11:15,312 --> 01:11:17,731
I was excited
about potential tasty treats.

1352
01:11:19,066 --> 01:11:21,318
They really went all out. What's all this?

1353
01:11:22,319 --> 01:11:23,529
When does it end?

1354
01:11:30,619 --> 01:11:31,912
Why are we going up so high?

1355
01:11:31,996 --> 01:11:33,330
It's a whole new journey.

1356
01:11:33,414 --> 01:11:34,707
All the others must be there.

1357
01:11:41,547 --> 01:11:42,631
It's one thing after another.

1358
01:11:45,801 --> 01:11:46,885
There's nothing here.

1359
01:11:48,470 --> 01:11:49,930
- Do we open this?
- I guess.

1360
01:11:50,556 --> 01:11:51,807
Why is it so heavy?

1361
01:11:58,105 --> 01:11:59,773
- What is this?
- Are we going outside?

1362
01:12:01,066 --> 01:12:02,109
What in the world is this?

1363
01:12:02,735 --> 01:12:03,861
Oh my.

1364
01:12:04,611 --> 01:12:05,612
What is all this?

1365
01:12:07,323 --> 01:12:09,325
This is unreal.

1366
01:12:09,408 --> 01:12:12,161
<i>Welcome to the exile zone.</i>

1367
01:13:51,385 --> 01:13:56,390
Subtitle translation by: Justin S. Kim
